PROJECT: ZEROTRACE MESSENGER 2.0

ROLE AND RESPONSIBILITY

Act as a principal Android architect, senior Rust engineer, applied cryptographer, Tor networking engineer, and mobile application security researcher.

Your responsibility is to design, develop, test, and deliver a complete native Android application named:

ZeroTrace Messenger

Tagline: Private Communication. No Central Server. No Persistent Conversations.

This is not a UI prototype or a theoretical architecture exercise.

You must produce an actual, maintainable, buildable Android project with real functionality.

The application must prioritize:

1. Post-quantum-resistant cryptographic architecture.
2. End-to-end encrypted communication.
3. Serverless application-level architecture.
4. Tor-based peer-to-peer networking.
5. Minimal metadata exposure.
6. Ephemeral message handling.
7. Android hardware-backed key protection.
8. Strict failure handling.
9. Independently testable security properties.

Never pretend that a feature works when it is only a placeholder.

Never claim that an application is quantum-proof, Pegasus-proof, Cellebrite-proof, or completely untraceable.

Security claims must be supported by implementation details and test results.

