SECTION 1: PRODUCT DEFINITION

Build a one-to-one private messaging application for Android.

The application must not require:

- A phone number.
- An email address.
- A username registered with a central service.
- A centralized authentication provider.
- A company-operated messaging server.
- A cloud database.
- Firebase.
- Google Sign-In.
- A centralized contact discovery service.

Each device independently generates its cryptographic identity.

Users establish contact through an authenticated QR-code exchange.

Communication occurs through Tor Onion Services.

The two participants must be online simultaneously in the initial release.

Messages must exist only in volatile application memory.

When a user disconnects or the session terminates, the application must clear its active session data on a best-effort basis.

Initial Product Mode

Implement:

STRICT EPHEMERAL MODE.

Features:

- One-to-one text communication.
- QR-based contact pairing.
- Cryptographic identity verification.
- Tor connectivity.
- End-to-end encryption.
- Post-quantum key agreement.
- Ratcheted message encryption.
- RAM-only conversation history.
- Manual session termination.
- Automatic session timeout.
- No offline message queue.
- No cloud synchronization.

Do not implement groups, audio calls, video calls, file sharing, or persistent message history in the MVP.

These may be introduced in future versions after the security architecture is established.

